module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.join_answers_with_one_arm_others_unjudged

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data join_answers_with_one_arm_others_unjudged: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "join_answers_with_one_arm_others_unjudged" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a join answers with ONE of its inputs, so the inputs it did not answer with are judged nowhere** (a reduction over several producers -- match arms, branch arms, any fold that collapses N types to one -- picks its answer by a tie-break and every downstream check then reads only that answer. ",

    "An input the fold did not select is compared with NOTHING: not with the join's answer, not with the consumer's declared type. ",

    "**THE TELL IS THAT THE VERDICT IS A FUNCTION OF INPUT ORDER**, and that is also the falsifier: permute the arms and re-run. ",

    "SPECIMEN, measured 2026-09-02 on gunbc, two modules identical except for arm order: v1.compiler.infer folded match arm body types through v1.compiler.infer_types prefer_specific_type, whose tie-break for two disjoint coproducts is the LEFT operand, so `match fl \{ FYes => FResA  FNo => FOthA \}` passed to a formal declared FRes was ACCEPTED, while the same module with those two arms swapped was REFUSED at the direct-call argument seam with `declared 'Coproduct(FRes)', produced 'Coproduct(FOth)'`. ",

    "One of those is wrong and it is the ACCEPTED one -- values inhabit their declared types is the ordinary compiler floor, which DESIGN section 4b puts BELOW the ladder rather than on a rung of it. ",

    "**RECOGNITION RULE: wherever a reduction answers with one of its inputs rather than with a judgment ABOUT them, ask what judges the inputs it discarded -- and if the answer is 'the consumer, which sees only the winner', the discarded inputs are unjudged by construction.** The shape hides because the seam that WOULD refuse demonstrably works: it refuses the other order, so every probe that happens to order the arms unluckily reports the compiler healthy. ",

    "BOUNDED AGAINST TWO NEIGHBOURS. ",

    "It is not `absorbing_fallback`: nothing failed and nothing widened, the fold answered confidently and correctly for its own purpose -- selecting the more specific of two types is what it is for. ",

    "It is not `selection_view_read_as_population` either, though it is that class's compiler-internal cousin: there a measured subset is read as the population, here a SELECTED REPRESENTATIVE is read as a judgment about the whole set. ",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the ladder (silent wrongness). ",

    "RUNG AFTER THE REPAIR: mechanically preventable -- v1.compiler.infer match_arm_join_diagnostics asks match_arm_types_are_disjoint_coproducts once per arm, with the RED and its three controls enrolled at test.claim.match_arm_join_disjoint_coproduct_witness_test; the invalid state stays writable and safety depends on that check executing. ",

    "CEILING: structurally guaranteed -- a join that produces a JUDGED type carrying every arm's verdict, rather than a representative selected from the arms, makes an unjudged arm unconstructible. ",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, a capability and not an artifact: one join relation that every N-ary join in the stage consumes, sufficient that no arm can reach a consumer without having been compared to the join's answer -- the ExprIf and ExprMatch joins in v1.compiler.infer are today two carriers asking two different questions of the same fold, which is what let one of them judge nothing at all.)\n\n**TWO FURTHER SPECIMENS, 2026-09-02 (quick-crab-396), BOTH FOUND WHILE MEASURING SOMETHING ELSE.** (1) v1.compiler.emit_rust `module_name_from_filename` reads `map_get(module_index.by_filename, mod_filename)` and resolves the resulting `List<TypedModule>` with `|> first`. ",

    "What makes it this class rather than an unlucky lookup is that the BUILDER KNOWS: `build_module_index` explicitly `list_push`es on collision, so the multiplicity is constructed deliberately and discarded silently by the reader, and the verdict is a function of fold order exactly as this row's recognition rule states. ",

    "The map compounds it by being keyed on `module_to_filename(module_NAME)` -- a filename DERIVED from the module name rather than the source path a declaration sits in -- so it answers the inverse question to the one its name suggests. ",

    "(2) v1.compiler.coercion `type_realization_decision` selects its checkpoint with `target_checkpoints(target) |> filter(cp => cp.dag_name == dag_name) |> first` -- a BARE-NAME filter resolved by first, standing inside the very function whose exact-identity rows (gunbc.rust_source_type_bindings) exist to remove that ambiguity. ",

    "The second specimen is the more valuable of the pair because it sits in the mechanism under repair rather than beside it.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
